            <ArticleTitle>Perioperative coronary spasm and right ventricular ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Perioperative coronary spasm after coronary bypass surgery is increasingly recognized as a possible cause of circulatory collapse. Most of the reported cases involved the right coronary artery (RCA). A case where transient right coronary spasm provoked right ventricular ischemia and collapse is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
